			<texPath>Things/Building/M127mmOtobredaC_Top_Indirect</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
		</graphicData>
		<description>The Otobreda 127/54C was an Italian naval gun developed for rapid-fire against surface and shore targets. It has an indirect fire variant, requires reloading after each shot, and is capable of settlement bombardment. Power: 350, HP: 6000, Cooldown: 5.0s, Range: 7-22000, Rate of Fire: 12 rounds per minute, Aimed Burst: 1, Reload Time: 1s. Ammunition: AP shell with 150 penetration.</description>
